---
import Layout from '../_Layout.astro';
import { BASE, articles, type Article } from '../_data';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return articles.map((a) => ({ params: { slug: a.slug }, props: { article: a } }));
}
const { article } = Astro.props as { article: Article };
const more = articles.filter((a) => a.slug !== article.slug).slice(0, 3);
---

<Layout title={article.title} description={article.excerpt}>
  <article class="section" style="padding-top: 40px">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={`${BASE}/articles/`}>Articles</a><span>/</span><span>{article.category}</span>
      </nav>
      <h1>{article.title}</h1>
      <p class="card-meta"><span>{article.author}</span><span>{article.date}</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap"><div class="ph cover" style="--ar: 21 / 9"><img src={`/formyson/images/${article.slug}.jpg`} alt={article.title} loading="eager" decoding="async" /></div></div>
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <div class="prose">
        <p><strong>{article.excerpt}</strong></p>
        <p>For years, the default playbook for a growing label was simple: design locally, produce overseas, wait. That math is changing. Freight volatility, higher minimums and the need to react mid-season have pushed more brands to look closer to home.</p>
        <h2>Speed is the new margin</h2>
        <p>When your design team and the sewing line share a building, a fit comment becomes a revised sample the same week. Read more in our <a href="#">production timeline guide</a>.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Sampling in 10 - 14 days</li>
          <li>Bulk in 4 - 6 weeks</li>
          <li>Reorders without re-quoting freight</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="ph" style="--ar: 16 / 9"><img src="/formyson/images/cutting.jpg" alt="Fabric being cut in the pattern room" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
        <blockquote>"We launched two drops in the time it used to take us to approve one sample."</blockquote>
        <h2>What to ask a domestic partner</h2>
        <p>Ask who owns the pattern, how QC is documented, and what happens when a trim is late. The answers tell you more than a price sheet. <a href={`${BASE}/contact/`}>Talk to our team</a> about your next program.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tags">
        <span class="chip">{article.category}</span><span class="chip">Manufacturing</span><span class="chip">Made in USA</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <section class="section more">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head"><div><h2>More articles</h2></div></div>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        {more.map((a) => (
          <a class="card" href={`${BASE}/articles/${a.slug}/`}>
            <div class="card-media"><div class="ph" style="--ar: 3 / 2"><img src={`/formyson/images/${a.slug}.jpg`} alt={a.title} loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div></div>
            <p class="card-meta"><span>{a.category}</span><span>{a.date}</span></p>
            <h3>{a.title}</h3>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 768px; display: grid; gap: 20px; }
  .narrow h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3.2rem); }
  .cover { margin: 48px 0; }
  .tags { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 32px; }
  .more { background: var(--surface); }
</style>
